{
  "description": "Shared project settings. RTK (Rust Token Killer) PreToolUse hook compresses noisy shell output (pytest/ruff/git/docker/...) before it reaches the agent context. Scoped by an allowlist in .claude/hooks/rtk-bash.sh; skips `uv run` and file reads. Requires `rtk` on PATH (winget install rtk-ai.rtk); no-ops silently if absent. plan-guard.mjs enforces work_plan.md §6's owner-gate registry and branch discipline deterministically — it is the layer that makes unattended dispatch safe; update it in the same PR as any §6 change. session-handoff.mjs (D39) injects project-docs/HANDOFF.md's open entries at session start, so cross-session work is carried by the repo instead of by the owner's memory; it fails open and silent. ste-lint.mjs holds the repo to Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100) — contract docs/style_ste.md, word list .claude/hooks/ste-words.json. It reads ONLY the text an agent just wrote to a markdown file, never the rest of the file, because the rule is a ratchet over 196 grandfathered docs (19094 errors, measured 2026-08-26); it fails open, unlike plan-guard.",
  "_permissions_note": [
    "DEV-PHASE POSTURE — owner directive 2026-09-01, expires 2026-09-30.",
    "Contract: CLAUDE.md §3a. Registry banner: work_plan.md §6.",
    "",
    "This list lives in the TRACKED settings file on purpose (D29). The same",
    "list sat in .claude/settings.local.json, which .gitignore excludes, so a",
    "cloud or headless session inherited none of it and prompted on every step.",
    "",
    "It is broad because the narrow version stopped at `bash`, `psql`, `curl`",
    "and `docker compose` — which is every step of the documented R8 database",
    "loop (`bash scripts/dev_db.sh`) and every diagnostic on the box.",
    "",
    "⚠️ AN ALLOW ENTRY DOES NOT BYPASS plan-guard.mjs. `Bash(ssh:*)` was already",
    "allowed while the guard still refused ssh. The two layers are independent:",
    "this one decides whether to prompt, the hook decides whether to permit.",
    "",
    "TO REVERT ON 2026-10-01: delete this note and the `permissions` block."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(ssh:*)", "Bash(scp:*)", "Bash(rsync:*)", "Bash(sftp:*)",
      "Bash(git:*)", "Bash(gh:*)",
      "Bash(bash:*)", "Bash(sh:*)", "Bash(zsh:*)", "Bash(make:*)",
      "Bash(uv:*)", "Bash(uvx:*)", "Bash(python:*)", "Bash(python3:*)",
      "Bash(pytest:*)", "Bash(ruff:*)", "Bash(mypy:*)", "Bash(alembic:*)",
      "Bash(npx:*)", "Bash(npm:*)", "Bash(node:*)", "Bash(pnpm:*)",
      "Bash(yarn:*)", "Bash(tsc:*)", "Bash(vitest:*)", "Bash(eslint:*)",
      "Bash(psql:*)", "Bash(pg_dump:*)", "Bash(pg_restore:*)",
      "Bash(pg_isready:*)", "Bash(supabase:*)", "Bash(redis-cli:*)",
      "Bash(docker:*)", "Bash(docker-compose:*)",
      "Bash(curl:*)", "Bash(wget:*)", "Bash(dig:*)", "Bash(nc:*)",
      "Bash(rg:*)", "Bash(ls:*)", "Bash(cat:*)", "Bash(head:*)", "Bash(tail:*)",
      "Bash(sed:*)", "Bash(awk:*)", "Bash(grep:*)", "Bash(find:*)", "Bash(wc:*)",
      "Bash(diff:*)", "Bash(cp:*)", "Bash(mv:*)", "Bash(mkdir:*)", "Bash(echo:*)",
      "Bash(printf:*)", "Bash(jq:*)", "Bash(yq:*)", "Bash(sort:*)", "Bash(uniq:*)",
      "Bash(cut:*)", "Bash(tr:*)", "Bash(xargs:*)", "Bash(tee:*)", "Bash(touch:*)",
      "Bash(chmod:*)", "Bash(ln:*)", "Bash(rm:*)", "Bash(tar:*)", "Bash(gzip:*)",
      "Bash(env:*)", "Bash(export:*)", "Bash(which:*)", "Bash(pwd:*)", "Bash(cd:*)",
      "Bash(test:*)", "Bash(date:*)", "Bash(sleep:*)", "Bash(timeout:*)",
      "Read", "Edit", "Write", "MultiEdit", "WebFetch", "WebSearch",
      "mcp__supabase__list_projects", "mcp__supabase__get_project",
      "mcp__supabase__get_project_url", "mcp__supabase__get_publishable_keys",
      "mcp__supabase__list_organizations", "mcp__supabase__get_organization",
      "mcp__supabase__list_tables", "mcp__supabase__list_migrations",
      "mcp__supabase__list_extensions", "mcp__supabase__execute_sql",
      "mcp__supabase__apply_migration", "mcp__supabase__query_logs",
      "mcp__supabase__get_advisors", "mcp__supabase__search_docs",
      "mcp__supabase__generate_typescript_types",
      "mcp__supabase__list_branches", "mcp__supabase__create_branch",
      "mcp__supabase__list_edge_functions", "mcp__supabase__get_edge_function",
      "mcp__supabase__deploy_edge_function",
      "mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Bash(rm -rf /:*)",
      "Bash(sudo rm:*)",
      "mcp__supabase__delete_branch",
      "mcp__supabase__pause_project",
      "mcp__hostinger-vps__VPS_recreateVirtualMachineV1",
      "mcp__hostinger-vps__VPS_restoreBackupV1",
      "mcp__hostinger-vps__VPS_restoreSnapshotV1",
      "mcp__hostinger-vps__VPS_setRootPasswordV1",
      "mcp__hostinger-domains__domains_startOutgoingDomainMoveV1",
      "mcp__hostinger-dns__DNS_resetDNSRecordsV1"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/session-handoff.mjs\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "handoff: loading pending work"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/worktree-notice.mjs\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "worktree: checking session isolation"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/rtk-bash.sh\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "rtk: compressing output"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash|PowerShell|Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/plan-guard.mjs\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "plan-guard: checking owner gates"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ste-lint.mjs\" --hook",
            "timeout": 15,
            "statusMessage": "ste-lint: checking the text just written"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
